---Describes the base virtual machine profile for fleet
---@class azure.azurefleet.BaseVirtualMachineProfile
---@field osProfile? azure.azurefleet.VirtualMachineScaleSetOSProfile Specifies the operating system settings for the virtual machines in the scale set.
---@field storageProfile? azure.azurefleet.VirtualMachineScaleSetStorageProfile Specifies the storage settings for the virtual machine disks.
---@field networkProfile? azure.azurefleet.VirtualMachineScaleSetNetworkProfile Specifies properties of the network interfaces of the virtual machines in the scale set.
---@field securityProfile? azure.azurefleet.SecurityProfile Specifies the Security related profile settings for the virtual machines in the scale set.
---@field diagnosticsProfile? azure.azurefleet.DiagnosticsProfile Specifies the boot diagnostic settings state.
---@field extensionProfile? azure.azurefleet.VirtualMachineScaleSetExtensionProfile Specifies a collection of settings for extensions installed on virtual machines in the scale set.
---@field licenseType? string Specifies that the image or disk that is being used was licensed on-premises. <br><br> Possible values for Windows Server operating system are: <br><br> Windows_Client <br><br> Windows_Server <br><br> Possible values for Linux Server operating system are: <br><br> RHEL_BYOS (for RHEL) <br><br> SLES_BYOS (for SUSE) <br><br> For more information, see [Azure Hybrid Use Benefit for Windows Server](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/virtual-machines/windows/hybrid-use-benefit-licensing) <br><br> [Azure Hybrid Use Benefit for Linux Server](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/virtual-machines/linux/azure-hybrid-benefit-linux) <br><br> Minimum api-version: 2015-06-15
