---Describes a virtual machine scale set data disk.
---@class azure.azurefleet.VirtualMachineScaleSetDataDisk
---@field name? string The disk name.
---@field lun number Specifies the logical unit number of the data disk. This value is used to identify data disks within the VM and therefore must be unique for each data disk attached to a VM.
---@field caching? azure.azurefleet.CachingTypes|string Specifies the caching requirements. Possible values are: **None,** **ReadOnly,** **ReadWrite.** The default values are: **None for Standard storage. ReadOnly for Premium storage.**
---@field writeAcceleratorEnabled? boolean Specifies whether writeAccelerator should be enabled or disabled on the disk.
---@field createOption azure.azurefleet.DiskCreateOptionTypes|string The create option.
---@field diskSizeGB? number Specifies the size of an empty data disk in gigabytes. This element can be used to overwrite the size of the disk in a virtual machine image. The property diskSizeGB is the number of bytes x 1024^3 for the disk and the value cannot be larger than 1023.
---@field managedDisk? azure.azurefleet.VirtualMachineScaleSetManagedDiskParameters The managed disk parameters.
---@field diskIOPSReadWrite? number Specifies the Read-Write IOPS for the managed disk. Should be used only when StorageAccountType is UltraSSD_LRS. If not specified, a default value would be assigned based on diskSizeGB.
---@field diskMBpsReadWrite? number Specifies the bandwidth in MB per second for the managed disk. Should be used only when StorageAccountType is UltraSSD_LRS. If not specified, a default value would be assigned based on diskSizeGB.
---@field deleteOption? azure.azurefleet.DiskDeleteOptionTypes|string Specifies whether data disk should be deleted or detached upon VMSS Flex deletion (This feature is available for VMSS with Flexible OrchestrationMode only).<br><br> Possible values: <br><br> **Delete** If this value is used, the data disk is deleted when the VMSS Flex VM is deleted.<br><br> **Detach** If this value is used, the data disk is retained after VMSS Flex VM is deleted.<br><br> The default value is set to **Delete**.

